    "inputs": "Base gateway, conditions and countermeasures from examples/paper/e2_infusion_pump_conditions.json. The original draft names the six conditions and their detecting agents (Table II) but not their configurations; the file reproduces the configurations of the v0.1.0 experiment script that produced the draft's numbers (kept with the manuscript sources, not part of this repository).",
    "conditions": "Each attacked configuration is the start configuration with the condition's changes. Every change set equals the effect of the simulator's attack injection named in simulator_attack (simulation/engine.py: Simulation.inject), recomputed here on a simulated device configured like the start configuration (results[].simulator_effect).",
    "assumptions": [
      "Base gateway: TLS 1.2, ECDHE-P256 key exchange, ECDSA-P256 certificate signature, RSA-2048 certificate key, AES-128-GCM, SHA-256, data lifetime 8 years, one authenticated device record and one benign AI prompt; default constraints (100,000 USD, 40 h) and assumptions (y = 5, z = 10, L = 10). The 8-year lifetime lies below L, so the classical baseline carries Mosca's medium finding (8 + 5 > 10) instead of the critical lifetime override.",
      "HNDL capture of long-lived data: data lifetime raised to 25 years (simulator hndl_capture: max(lifetime, 25)).",
      "Legacy-fallback downgrade: TLS 1.0, RSA key transport and SHA-1 (simulator tls_downgrade).",
      "Classical-only group fallback: starts from the migrated gateway (the base gateway after the countermeasures, applied by code) and drops the ML-KEM share, key exchange ECDHE-P256 (simulator pq_strip, which needs an ML-KEM share to drop).",
      "Certificate-forgery attempt (named 'Quantum certificate forgery' in the v0.1.0 script): device record without certificate, failed authentication, 6 failed logins; the certificate signature is already the classical ECDSA-P256 (simulator cert_spoof).",
      "PQ-downgrade prompt injection: the simulator's pq_downgrade_prompt text appended to the AI prompt log.",
      "Countermeasures (Section V-C): the catalogue mitigations enable_hybrid_mlkem, pq_certificates, upgrade_tls13, strong_hash, pq_policy_pinning, device_reauth and prompt_firewall, applied to every attacked configuration with optimizer.reassess.apply_plan. The result equals the v0.1.0 'defended profile' (TLS 1.3, X25519MLKEM768, ML-DSA-65 certificate signature and key, AES-256-GCM, SHA-384, re-authenticated device, downgrade prompt removed); pq_policy_pinning has no configuration fields and is applied as a no-op."
    ],
    "assessment": "Before and after: one full pipeline run each, seed 2026, default options, no LLM. 'Detected by' is the set of agents that raised at least one finding."
  },
